{
  "text": " Thank you for being with us. We will go into recess to hear from our physicians. Just let us know who you are and who you represent, just like your mom used to tell you when you went out on a date. Just remember who you represent. Thank you, Mr. Chairman. Thank you, committee. So my name is Dr. Paul Merrick. I'm a scientist. I'm a researcher and a clinician. I practice critical care medicine for 35 years. I have been treating COVID-19 since March of 2020, not to self-promote myself. I am the second most published critical care person ever in the world. We developed in March 2020 a protocol for the treatment of COVID-19. This was first the Eastern Virginia Medical School protocol, which then morphed into the FLCC protocol for the prevention, early treatment, hospital treatment, and treatment of post-COVID syndrome. This protocol has been downloaded over 10 million times and is probably one of the most widely used protocols in the world. It's used in many countries as their definitive protocol. So we're talking about ivermectin. So ivermectin is a natural compound which was found in a golf course in Japan. So this is a natural product. It is truly a remarkable drug in that it treats parasitic diseases and RNA viruses. So there was some dispute about whether it treats RNA viruses. So we know for 10 years this compound is active against chikungunya, dengue, influenza, and SARS-CoV-2 virus. It acts via a number of different mechanisms to prevent replication of this virus. It's probably one of the safest medications ever made. So just for the record it's been over 3.7 billion people have been given ivermectin for the treatment of parasitic diseases in Africa, Asia, and South America. It's completely changed the face of parasitic diseases on this planet. After penicillin it is that drug which has had the greatest impact on humanity. It is extremely safe. More people have died from Tylenol than from ivermectin, which is important to stress. In terms of COVID, one couldn't have asked for nature to give us a more perfect drug, because it kills the virus, the replicating virus via a number of mechanisms, and it also has potent anti-inflammatory properties. So it really is the perfect drug for the treatment of COVID-19. It's been demonstrated in multiple randomized controlled trials, the over 71 trials, probably 50 randomized controlled trials, showing that it is effective in prophylaxis, it decreases time of symptoms, it decreases hospitalization, and it decreases mortality by 50%. I was just texted a paper this morning that was published today in a well-known reputable medical journal that compared the mortality benefit of remdesivir versus ivermectin. The results left remdesivir completely out of the water. So this drug was 70 times more potent in reducing deaths from ivermectin, I mean from COVID-19. It works across the spectrum of disease. As you know, there has been a willful intention of propaganda to dismiss this drug, to call it a toxic horse deworming medicine, to invalidate its potent antiviral activity. It probably is the most effective drug against SARS-CoV-2. Let me say that because it's so important. This drug is probably the most effective drug against SARS-CoV-2 and has a safety profile better than Tylenol. And it's an outrage that there's been such profound propaganda to limit its use, to silence doctors who prescribe it, to prevent pharmacists from dispensing it. If we had utilized our protocol, which we had published in March of 2020, it's my belief we could have saved hundreds of thousands of lives. Because the key to COVID is early treatment. It's early treatment. This is a treatable disease. And if you treat the patients early, you prevent transmission of the disease. You prevent progression of the disease. You prevent admission to hospital. And you prevent death. From my point of view, it's perplexing that this drug has not been regarded as the drug to treat COVID. Now, clearly what I need to emphasize is that no magic bullet. This drug is used in combination with other drugs. But it's part of our protocol being a major component. So, you know, that's just a brief synopsis on ivermectin. If there are any questions, I'd be happy to answer. Thank you. And I think Dr. Sibley has treated somewhere around 4,000 patients free of charge trying to help. We appreciate that.",
